POINT 7 -- marker (.encrypted) and verification (.encryption-verify) files are
correctly excluded.  CONFIRMED INDEPENDENTLY, not inherited.
  (a) Static: every touch of them is a raw syscall, never the caching reader.
      $ grep -rn 'markerFile|verifyFile' --include=*.go . | grep -v _test.go
        migration.go:44,49 os.WriteFile(verifyPath)  migration.go:101-102
        os.WriteFile(markerPath)  migration.go:143 os.ReadFile(verifyPath)
        migration.go:192 os.Remove  storage.go:90 os.Stat  storage.go:162
        os.ReadFile
  (b) Call-graph: the four places that could pass an attacker- or
      user-influenced path to Storage.ReadFile/OpenFile cannot reach them.
      - backup plaintext export (handlers.go:406 store.OpenFile) is gated by
        backupsvc.SkipPredicate, whose last statement is
        `return storage.IsEncryptionStateFile(base)` (snapshot.go:277).
      - explorer import readBack (handlers.go:566) rejects any name without a
        .csv suffix before any filesystem access (handlers.go:643-645).
      - retirement scenariosReferencingFile globs "whatif*.json".
      - SharedTx.ReadFile just delegates to Storage.ReadFile.
  (c) Dynamic: I instrumented a scratch copy, printing PROBE_ lines from the
      top of ReadFileContext and from publishCache whenever
      IsEncryptionStateFile(base) held, then ran the WHOLE repo suite:
      $ go test -count=1 ./...  -> suite_exit=0, grep -c PROBE_ -> 0
      Zero reaches, repo-wide.
  (d) Migration never rewrites them either:
      shouldSkipEncryption(.encrypted)=true, (.encryption-verify)=true,
      (.encryption-config.json)=true  (scratch test, all three logged true).
  Recorded qualification: ReadFileContext applies no base-name exclusion of its
  own. A scratch probe calling s.ReadFile(markerPath) / s.ReadFile(verifyPath)
  directly logged "marker cached ... true" and "verify cached ... true". The
  exclusion is therefore sound but rests on caller discipline, not on a guard.
  No such caller exists today, so the exclusion is not a defect -- it is a
  property that a future caller could silently break.

